<title>NEW ZEALAND: Mainfreight half year profit up 27 pct.</title>
<headline>Mainfreight half year profit up 27 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year result to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    2.01 vs 1.58</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   3.35 vs 30.38</p>
<p>    Div (cents)			    2.5 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Turnover			     69.38 vs 64.34</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			 3.29 vs 2.52</p>
<p>    Tax				     1.14 vs 0.85</p>
<p>    Abnormals before tax		0.53 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)   57.77 vs n/a</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credit.</p>
<p>Pay date Dec 13</p>
<p>Reg date Dec 6</p>
<p>    Ex div   Dec 9</p>
<p>Note - Mainfreight Ltd is a freight forwarding and distribution company. Mainfreight said its flotation in June this year resulted in an abnormal cost of NZ$526,000 before tax.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
